  "schema_version": "axiom-oracles/taxsim-pin/v2",
  "description": "Pinned identity of every NBER TAXSIM (taxsimtest) executable the axiom-oracles TAXSIM adapter may run. `binaries` pins each executable by SHA-256 and byte size, with the NBER build stamp read from its bytes and the sources it can be fetched from (pinned git blobs, NBER URLs, PyPI wheels). `profiles` map every (TAXSIM SOI state, tax year) to one pinned binary per platform: a profile default plus declarative overrides. `default_profile` is the one field to change when the benchmark moves to a different binary vintage. The adapter hashes each binary before executing it and refuses any bytes that do not match (axiom_oracles/adapters/taxsim/pins.py). `distribution` pins the policyengine-taxsim package that supplies the Python wrapper (input formatting, output parsing) and the PolicyEngine emulator; its bundled executables are recorded for the callers that still run them directly.",
